The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (dm_cell_unlock_v2(cache->prison, mg->cell, &bios))
	free_prison_cell(cache, mg->cell);
Reason:
When `mg->cell` is NULL (e.g., due to a failed bio prison cell lock in passthrough mode), these lines unconditionally dereference the pointer in `dm_cell_unlock_v2` and `free_prison_cell`, causing a null-pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (mg->cell) {
	if (dm_cell_unlock_v2(cache->prison, mg->cell, &bios))
		free_prison_cell(cache, mg->cell);
}
Reason:
The added `if (mg->cell)` guard ensures that the cell unlocking and freeing operations are only performed when `mg->cell` is non‑NULL, thus avoiding the null‑pointer dereference in the error path.

